Title: make data exits 255 on a run_report with no hash info in dvc.lock
Created: 2026-07-27
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-07-27T18:32Z HDMX-coding-agent created
2026-07-27T18:35Z HDMX-coding-agent note found while verifying 0360's shared-cache fix end to end in a probe worktree

--- body ---
## Context

With 0360's shared-cache fix in place, `make data` in a fresh worktree does
check the corpus out of the primary cache — and still exits non-zero:

    $ make data
    uv run --env-file .env dvc checkout
    WARNING: No file hash info found for '.../data/catalogs/run_reports/catalog_merge.json'.
             It won't be created.
    ERROR: Checkout failed for following targets:
    data/catalogs/run_reports
    data/catalogs/run_reports/catalog_merge.json
    Is your cache up to date?
    make: *** [Makefile:203 : data] Erreur 255

Everything else lands: `citations.csv` (386 MB), `refined_works.csv`,
`enriched_works.csv`, `embeddings.npz` and the rest are all present. Only the
one run-report entry has no hash recorded.

This is *not* 0360's bug — that one was an empty private cache, now fixed and
verified. This is a separate gap in the recorded state, and it stayed masked
while `make data` could not work in a worktree at all.

## Why it matters

`make data` is the documented way to populate a worktree, and 0360's whole
point was to make that path usable. A target that does the work and then
returns 255 breaks anything chaining off it, and it trains the reader to ignore
a red exit code — which is how the next real checkout failure gets waved
through.

## Relevant files

- `dvc.lock` — the `outs` entry for `data/catalogs/run_reports`
- `Makefile:203` — the `data:` target
- `scripts/pipeline_io.py` — `save_run_report`, which writes the run reports
- `tickets/closed/0360-*.erg` — the shared-cache fix that surfaced this

## Actions

1. Establish whether `catalog_merge.json` is missing from the cache or present
   but unrecorded in `dvc.lock`. `dvc status` plus a direct look at the
   recorded `outs` entry separates the two.
2. If the artifact is genuinely stale or absent, regenerate or `dvc commit` it
   and push, so recorded state and cache agree.
3. Decide whether run reports belong in the checkout contract at all. They are
   QA summaries, not corpus data; if a missing one should not fail `make data`,
   the fix is to scope the target rather than to chase the file.

## Test

Integration, in a fresh worktree, asserting the exit code and not just the
files — the current failure is invisible to any check that only looks for
`refined_works.csv`:

    git -c core.hooksPath=.githooks worktree add <tmp> --detach HEAD
    cd <tmp> && make data          # must exit 0
    test -f data/catalogs/refined_works.csv

## Verification

- [ ] `make data` in a fresh worktree exits 0
- [ ] `dvc status` reports the run_reports out as clean
- [ ] The corpus files still check out byte-identically

## Invariants

- No corpus artifact is regenerated to satisfy this — the contract files are
  already correct and must not be touched.
- Whatever lands keeps `make data` network-free.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make data` succeeds end to end in a worktree with a zero exit code, or
      the run-report out is deliberately removed from what that target checks
      out, with the reason recorded here.
